From: Surface Pro X Linux Project <minseokkim1020@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI/ACPI: Keep consumer memory resources as host bridge
 windows on WoA devices

Qualcomm Windows-on-ARM machines (Microsoft Surface Pro X among others)
describe PCIe host bridge windows as Memory32Fixed "consumer"
descriptors in the PNP0A03 _CRS instead of producer descriptors.

Commit 8fd4391ee717 ("arm64: PCI: Exclude ACPI "consumer" resources
from host bridge windows") makes the kernel drop every non-window
resource entry while preparing host bridge resources. On these
machines that removes the only memory window the firmware provides, so
BAR assignment fails ("BAR 0: failed to assign [mem ...]") and PCIe
devices — most visibly the NVMe SSD — show up in lspci but never bind
a driver.

Add a DMI-matched quirk that converts consumer memory descriptors into
host bridge windows instead of destroying them on affected machines.

This only matters for the ACPI boot path; Device Tree boot is
unaffected. Approach follows Shawn Guo's proposal ("arm64: PCI: Add
quirk for Qualcomm WoA devices", 2023-04), which as of mainline 2026
has not landed: drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c still destroys all non-window
entries unconditionally.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20230423030520.9570-1-shawn.guo@linaro.org/
diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c b/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c
index 4d0f2cb..35ad393 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/irqdomain.h>
@@ -1591,14 +1592,40 @@ int pcibios_root_bridge_prepare(struct pci_host_bridge *bridge)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Qualcomm Windows-on-ARM firmware describes host bridge windows as
+ * Memory32Fixed "consumer" descriptors in the PNP0A03 _CRS. Dropping
+ * them leaves the bridge without memory windows and BAR assignment
+ * fails for every device behind it (NVMe, Wi-Fi, WWAN).
+ */
+static const struct dmi_system_id woa_consumer_window_quirk_table[] = {
+	{
+		/* Microsoft Surface Pro X (SQ1 and SQ2) */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Microsoft Corporation"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Surface Pro X"),
+		},
+	},
+	{ }
+};
+
 static int pci_acpi_root_prepare_resources(struct acpi_pci_root_info *ci)
 {
 	struct resource_entry *entry, *tmp;
+	bool keep_consumer_mem;
 	int status;
 
+	keep_consumer_mem = dmi_check_system(woa_consumer_window_quirk_table);
+
 	status = acpi_pci_probe_root_resources(ci);
 	resource_list_for_each_entry_safe(entry, tmp, &ci->resources) {
-		if (!(entry->res->flags & IORESOURCE_WINDOW))
+		if (entry->res->flags & IORESOURCE_WINDOW)
+			continue;
+
+		if (keep_consumer_mem &&
+		    resource_type(entry->res) == IORESOURCE_MEM)
+			entry->res->flags |= IORESOURCE_WINDOW;
+		else
 			resource_list_destroy_entry(entry);
 	}
 	return status;
